  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT bilateral funding to World Health Organization (WHO) Country Office PNG 2025 - 2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment provides bilateral funding to the WHO Country Office PNG, and covers calendar years 2025 - 2028. It will fund five core technical positions in the WHO Country Office PNG, as well as activities across strategic objectives that mirror the priorities set out in the Papua New Guinea-WHO Country Cooperation Strategy 2024-2028 which are aligned to the PNG National Health Plan:
a)	Resilient systems for health;
b)	Healthier populations and non-communicable diseases;
c)	Integrated health services delivery targeted to high priority diseases; and
d)	Health security</narrative>
  </description>
